                <pb facs="0810" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1822</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October 7,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 11.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 281</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram of October
                    5th, 8 P.M. No. 295,<anchor n="71" xml:id="d742-f1"/> I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith the text of the agreement signed by the Ministry of
                    Communications of the Chinese Government, Yeh Kung Cho, and the Russo-Asiatic
                    Bank represented by Messrs. Jezierski and Raindre on the 2nd instant regarding
                    the Chinese Eastern Railway. This text was given me in confidence by the Russian
                    Minister and the Bank. I regret that the <pb facs="0811" n="713" xml:id="pg713"
                    /> shortness of time before the despatch of the pouch prevents the inclusion of
                    an English translation of the text.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For the Minister)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. B.
                            Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>





















